{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls7_jpg\\hist\\086.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "Unit:05TheMughal Empire", "conf": 0.909, "box": [[350, 97], [546, 101], [546, 121], [350, 117]]}, {"text": "Internal trade taxes wereabolished.", "conf": 0.924, "box": [[115, 121], [423, 131], [422, 154], [114, 144]]}, {"text": "buildingof Sarai (inns)fortravelers.", "conf": 0.926, "box": [[117, 175], [421, 182], [420, 204], [116, 197]]}, {"text": "Kabul was rebuilt.", "conf": 0.903, "box": [[117, 225], [272, 229], [272, 252], [116, 249]]}, {"text": "Do You Know?", "conf": 0.865, "box": [[103, 308], [252, 311], [252, 335], [103, 333]]}, {"text": "Qila Rohtas was built by Sher Shah Suri in 16th century. It is located on GT Road", "conf": 0.905, "box": [[100, 341], [787, 337], [787, 370], [100, 374]]}, {"text": "architecture in Subcontinent.", "conf": 0.913, "box": [[104, 395], [350, 395], [350, 419], [104, 419]]}, {"text": "Sher Shah Suri lost his life in an accident during the siege of Kalinjar fort in Uttar Perdesh", "conf": 0.948, "box": [[67, 489], [824, 484], [824, 515], [67, 520]]}, {"text": "on May 13, 1545 AD. Sher Shah Suri's successors, however, proved to be weak and", "conf": 0.894, "box": [[68, 518], [827, 512], [827, 542], [68, 548]]}, {"text": "incapablerulers.The Mughals wereabletoestablishtheirrules in India afterafewdays.", "conf": 0.919, "box": [[68, 545], [789, 540], [789, 566], [68, 571]]}, {"text": "Restoration of the Mughal Empire", "conf": 0.876, "box": [[67, 588], [452, 588], [452, 617], [67, 617]]}, {"text": "Humayun's Victoryand Death", "conf": 0.888, "box": [[66, 627], [323, 625], [323, 648], [66, 650]]}, {"text": "Humayun took advantage of the disputes among Sher Shah Suri's successors and returned", "conf": 0.93, "box": [[66, 660], [822, 652], [822, 679], [66, 688]]}, {"text": "to India. He recaptured Lahore, Delhiand Agra and regained the throne in 1555 AD with the", "conf": 0.894, "box": [[65, 687], [821, 677], [821, 704], [65, 713]]}, {"text": "helpof the emperor of Persia,Shah Tahmasp-I.Humayun made Delhi his capital and", "conf": 0.889, "box": [[66, 713], [819, 704], [819, 727], [66, 736]]}, {"text": "immediatelybegan toreorganizehis empire.Sixmonths afterregainingpower,hefell down", "conf": 0.908, "box": [[66, 737], [819, 728], [819, 752], [66, 762]]}, {"text": "thestairs ofhis libraryin Delhianddied.Hewas succeeded byhis son Akbar.", "conf": 0.926, "box": [[66, 763], [684, 755], [684, 779], [66, 786]]}, {"text": "JalaludDinMuhammadAkbar", "conf": 0.925, "box": [[65, 812], [402, 809], [403, 833], [65, 836]]}, {"text": "(1556AD-1605AD)", "conf": 0.905, "box": [[66, 843], [302, 838], [302, 868], [66, 873]]}, {"text": "During theyears of Humayun's exile in Persia,Akbar was raised", "conf": 0.892, "box": [[66, 885], [582, 877], [582, 900], [66, 908]]}, {"text": "among toughwarriors in Afghanistan.Although he could not", "conf": 0.894, "box": [[65, 910], [583, 901], [583, 924], [65, 933]]}, {"text": "learn to read and write formally but he was eager to acquire", "conf": 0.905, "box": [[65, 933], [582, 926], [582, 949], [65, 957]]}, {"text": "newideasfrompeoplewhovisited hiscourt.", "conf": 0.942, "box": [[65, 959], [438, 950], [439, 974], [65, 982]]}, {"text": "Humayun's Death", "conf": 0.882, "box": [[641, 983], [770, 981], [771, 1004], [641, 1006]]}, {"text": "Note for Teachers", "conf": 0.882, "box": [[175, 1028], [324, 1026], [324, 1048], [176, 1050]]}, {"text": "Inform the students that Sher Shah Suri was an eficient administrator and a", "conf": 0.93, "box": [[172, 1049], [768, 1042], [768, 1066], [173, 1072]]}, {"text": "brave militarygeneral.He was given the title\"Sher\"after he single-handedly", "conf": 0.881, "box": [[171, 1068], [767, 1063], [767, 1086], [172, 1091]]}, {"text": "killed a tiger.Sher Shah Suri is considered amongst the greatest Muslim rulers", "conf": 0.902, "box": [[171, 1086], [767, 1082], [767, 1106], [172, 1110]]}, {"text": "of the Subcontinent.", "conf": 0.874, "box": [[172, 1108], [324, 1104], [324, 1125], [173, 1130]]}, {"text": "81", "conf": 0.666, "box": [[422, 1148], [438, 1148], [438, 1161], [422, 1161]]}]}